"summary": "The Lean theorem states that there is a universal constant C > 0 with the following property. For every k ≥ 1 and every loopless multigraph on n ≥ 2 vertices with labelled edge copies that is k-edge-connected, some spanning tree T satisfies |δ_T(S)| ≤ (C/k)|δ_G(S)| for every cut ∅ ≠ S ⊊ V. The definitions are faithful. The most important caveat is that this is only the existence statement (the companion strong thin-tree conjecture). The paper's actual contribution, a deterministic polynomial-time algorithm that also handles binary-encoded multiplicities, is not formalized.",
